"en"}, {"gloss": "a numeral, Prāt.; Pāṇ. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(in gram.) number (as expressed by case terminations or personal t˚), Kāś. on Pāṇ. ii, 3, 1", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "deliberation, reasoning, reflection, reason, intellect, MBh.; Kāv.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "name, appellation (= आख्या), R.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "a partic. high number, Buddh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "manner, MW.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "(in geom.) a gnomon (for ascertaining the points of the compass), RāmRās.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सङ्ख्या"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saNKyA"]}, {"id": "saMKya", "headword": "संख्य", "headword_slp1": "saMKya", "fold": "sanKya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-ख्य mfn. counting up or over, reckoning or summing up, Pāṇ. iii, 2, 7, Sch. (ifc.; cf. गो-स्˚)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-ख्य m. N. of a man, Cat.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं-ख्य n. conflict, battle, war (only in loc.; cf. Naigh. ii, 17), MBh.; Kāv.; Rājat.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["संख्यं", "सङ्ख्य", "सङ्ख्यं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saMKyaM", "saNKya", "saNKyaM"]}, {"id": "sAMKya", "headword": "सांख्य", "headword_slp1": "sAMKya", "fold": "sanKya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सांख्य mfn. (fr. सं-ख्या) numeral, relating to number, W.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "relating to number (in gram. as expressed by the case-terminations &c.), Pat.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "rational, or discriminative, W.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सांख्य m. one who calculates or discriminates well, (esp.) an adherent of the Sāṃkhya doctrine, CūlUp.; MBh. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of a man, Car.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "patr. of the Vedic Ṛṣi Atri, Anukr.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "N. of Śiva, MBh.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सांख्य n. (accord. to some also m.) N. of one of the three great divisions of Hindū philosophy (ascribed to the sage Kapila [q.v.], and so called either from ‘discriminating’, in general, or, more probably, from ‘reckoning up’ or ‘enumerating’ twenty-five Tattvas [see तत्त्व] or true entities [twenty-three of which are evolved out of Prakṛti ‘the primordial Essence’ or ‘first-Producer’], viz. Buddhi, Ahaṃkāra, the five Tan-mātras, the five Mahā-bhūtas and Manas;\nthe twenty-fifth being Puruṣa or Spirit [sometimes called Soul] which is neither a Producer nor Production [see विकार], but wholly distinct from the twenty-four other Tattvas, and is multitudinous, each separate Puruṣa by its union with Prakṛti causing a separate creation out of Prakṛti, the object of the philosophy being to effect the final liberation of the Puruṣa or Spirit from the fetters caused by that creation;\nthe Yoga [q.v.] branch of the Sāṃkhya recognizes a Supreme Spirit dominating each separate Puruṣa;\nthe Tantras identify Prakṛti with the wives of the gods, esp. with the wife of Śiva;\nthe oldest systematic exposition of the S˚ seems to have been by an author called Pañca-śikha [the germ, however, being found in the Ṣaṣṭi-tantra, of which only scanty fragments are extant];\nthe original Sūtras were superseded by the S˚ of Īśvara-kṛṣṇa, the oldest manual on the S˚ system that has come down to us and probably written in the 5th century A.D., while the S˚-sūtras or Ś˚ and Tattva-samāsa, ascribed to the sage Kapila, are now thought to belong to as late a date as the 14th or 15th century or perhaps a little later), ŚvetUp.;\nMBh. &c., IW. 73 &c.;\nRTL.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सांख्यं", "सांख्यः", "साङ्ख्य", "साङ्ख्यः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sAMKyaM", "sAMKyaH", "sANKya", "sANKyaH"]}], "sanKyata": [{"id": "saMKyatA", "headword": "संख्यता", "headword_slp1": "saMKyatA", "fold": "sanKyata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-ख्य—ता f. numerableness, numeration, MW.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सङ्ख्यता"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saNKyatA"]}, {"id": "saMKyAta", "headword": "संख्यात", "headword_slp1": "saMKyAta", "fold": "sanKyata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं॑-ख्यात mfn. reckoned up, enumerated, numbered, counted, measured, AV. &c. &c.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "estimated by, R.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "considered (see comp.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं॑-ख्यात m. pl. N. of a people, VarBṛS.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "सं॑-ख्यात n. number, multitude, BhP.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सङ्ख्यात", "सङ्ख्यातं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saNKyAta", "saNKyAtaM"]}, {"id": "saMKyAtA", "headword": "संख्याता", "headword_slp1": "saMKyAtA", "fold": "sanKyata", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं॑-ख्याता (आ), f. (scil. प्रहेलिका) a kind of riddle based on counting, Kāv. iii, 101", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sanKyatva": [{"id": "saMKyatva", "headword": "संख्यत्व", "headword_slp1": "saMKyatva", "fold": "sanKyatva", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-ख्य—त्व n. numerableness, numeration, MW.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sanKyaka": [{"id": "saMKyaka", "headword": "संख्यक", "headword_slp1": "saMKyaka", "fold": "sanKyaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "सं-˚ख्यक mfn. numbering, amounting to (ifc.; cf. सहस्र-स्˚).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["सङ्ख्यक"], "synonyms_slp1": ["saNKyaka"]}, {"id": "saMKyAka", "headword": "संख्याक", "headword_slp1": "saMKyAka", "fold": "sanKyaka", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "mw-cologne", "senses": [{"gloss": "संख्याक mfn. amounting to (ifc., e.g. सप्तति-स्˚, q.v.), Hariv.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sanKyakOmudi": [{"id": "saMKyAkOmudI", "headword": "संख्याकौमुदी", "headword_slp1": "saMKyAkOmudI", "fold": "sanKyakOmudi", "headword_langu